Vim 7.4.1398 for DOS (DJGPP, 32-bit, needs DPMI: vmdos's own), on C: only
(the boot floppy has no room). VI.BAT runs it as vi.

  bin/VIM.EXE        github.com/vim/vim tag v7.4.1398, the last with the DJGPP
                     makefile (src/Make_djg.mak); DJGPP gcc 12, "normal"
                     features (syntax coloring, undo, search/replace, :s, ...),
                     UPX --best
  bin/VI.BAT         @C:\VMDOS\VIM.EXE %1 ... %9
  RT/_VIMRC          vmdos's settings (nocompatible, backspace, ruler, syntax on)
  RT/VIM74/          a few runtime files from the same tag: filetype detection
                     and syntax files for C/C++, assembler, batch, INI, make,
                     shell, Python, Pascal, BASIC, HTML/XML/CSS, Markdown, ...
                     (names kept to 8.3). No :help files (too big).
  vim-7.4.1398-djgpp.patch   what it takes to build with today's DJGPP:
                     json.o in the makefile, reltimefloat() only with
                     FEAT_FLOAT, EMPTY_IF_NULL's type
  LICENSE.txt        Vim's licence (runtime/doc/uganda.txt): charityware,
                     GPL-compatible

RT/ goes in C:\VMDOS: Vim looks for $VIM\_VIMRC and $VIM\VIM74 and, with no
VIM variable set, takes $VIM to be its own directory. More syntax files: copy
them from any Vim 7.4 runtime/syntax into C:\VMDOS\VIM74\SYNTAX (8.3 names,
or with DOSLFN loaded, any).

tools/build-vim.sh rebuilds bin/VIM.EXE (same size; only the build date in
:version differs).

Exiting Vim under QEMU without KVM used to crash QEMU (8.2's TCG matches a
DR0 breakpoint against EIP, not the linear address, and DJGPP's code segment
isn't based at 0): src/dpmi.c now single-steps such segments under TCG.
